# Overlay & Rendering

## Thread model

- **Main tick** (`RadarApp`): memory reads, hotkeys, builds `RenderContext`, publishes via volatile/ref swap.
- **ImGui thread** (STA, `ImGuiRadarOverlay`): consumes `RenderContext`, draws only — **no** `MemoryReader` calls in `Render()`.
- **World thread** (`WorldReaderLoop`): heavy entity/terrain walk → `WorldSnapshot`.

Never block the render thread on memory I/O or pathfinding.

## RenderContext / WorldSnapshot

- Immutable-ish snapshots passed to render; use `Array.Empty<T>()` for cleared state.
- World-rate data (entities, terrain, paths) from `WorldSnapshot`; frame-rate data (player, map lock) from live frame.
- Item labels / HP bars: spec from world tick; overlay may re-read **live position only** for smooth follow.

## Draw policy

- Skip overlay when game unfocused unless `AlwaysShowOverlay`.
- Respect per-layer toggles (`ShowPathWorld`, `ShowPathMap`, `MapOverlayDrawPolicy`, etc.).
- Style from `RadarSettings` — colors, sizes, opacity, shapes via `IconAtlas` / `SpriteIconRef`.
- Anchor to game **client rect** (`GetClientRect` + `ClientToScreen`), not outer window rect.

## ImGui conventions

- `ImGuiConfigFlags.NoMouseCursorChange` — don't steal cursor from game.
- `OverlayVSync` user-tunable; record segment timings in `OverlayRenderMetrics` when adding heavy draw passes.

## Assets

- Built-in SVG icons → `IconLibrary.MaterializeTo` on first run; user overrides in `icons/`.
- Texture atlas via `IconAtlas` / `TextureRegistry` — don't load per-frame.
